IMPORT prelude

-- Prevention of Human Trafficking Act 2014 (Singapore) -- what counts as trafficking and what it costs: the definitions a case turns
-- on (s 2: child, abuse of the position of vulnerability, exploitation, debt bondage), the trafficking offence (s 3), the penalties and
-- the listed aggravating factors (s 4), abetment (s 5), receiving payments (s 6), the 48-hour limit on arrest without warrant
-- (s 9(3)), the offence penalties in ss 17, 18 and 20, the protection of sexually-exploited victims (s 18) and of informers (s 21).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation marked
-- "version in force from 17/8/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PHTA2014.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 21 of 2025 (Criminal Law (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2025) "wef 17/08/2026", against s 4(1) and s 6(2). The deposit does
-- not show what those penalties were before that amendment.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. REQ-0058 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life relevance.
-- The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Act is short (24 sections), so the row covers nearly all of the rules a person can be on either side of. Not encoded: the
-- other s 2 definitions beyond their use here (servile form of marriage, serfdom, servitude are named, not tested), the enforcement
-- powers in ss 7, 8 and 10 to 16 except where s 8(4) feeds s 17, bail (s 9(4), (5)), the "reasonable in the circumstances" limb of
-- s 9(3), victim assistance (s 19, which is discretionary), the elements of the s 20 false-statement offence (only its penalty),
-- the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 22), District Court jurisdiction to impose the full penalty (s 23), and rules (s 24). Caning exemptions under other Acts are not in this Act
-- and are not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Prevention of Human Trafficking Act 2014 -- offences`

§§ `2 -- definitions`

-- "child" means an individual below 18 years of age.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child` IF age LESS THAN 18

-- "abuse of the position of vulnerability" MEANS taking advantage of the vulnerable position the individual is placed in "as a result
-- of" (a) entering or remaining in Singapore illegally; (b) pregnancy; (c) physical or mental illness, infirmity or disability; or
-- (d) impairment of decision-making ability by reason of such illness, infirmity or disability. The list is closed ("means"):
-- poverty, debt or being a lawful foreign worker are not on it (they may still be coercion or debt bondage on other facts).
DECLARE Vulnerability IS ONE OF
    `entering or remaining in Singapore illegally`
    `pregnancy`
    `illness, infirmity or disability`
    `impaired decision-making from illness or disability`
    `poverty`
    `being a lawful foreign worker`

GIVEN `the vulnerability` IS A Vulnerability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a position of vulnerability under s 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the vulnerability`
    WHEN `poverty` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `being a lawful foreign worker` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "debt bondage": (a) "the pledging by a debtor of the personal services of the debtor or an individual under the debtor's control,
-- as security for a debt"; AND (b) "the reasonable value of such services not being applied towards the discharge of the debt, or
-- the length or nature of such services not being limited or defined". Debt bondage is a "practice similar to slavery", which is
-- exploitation.
GIVEN `services pledged as security for a debt` IS A BOOLEAN, `value applied towards the debt` IS A BOOLEAN, `length and nature defined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is debt bondage` IF
    `services pledged as security for a debt` AND ((NOT `value applied towards the debt`) OR (NOT `length and nature defined`))

-- "exploitation" means "sexual exploitation, forced labour, slavery or any practice similar to slavery, servitude or the removal of
-- an organ".
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `sexual exploitation`
    `forced labour`
    `slavery`
    `a practice similar to slavery`
    `servitude`
    `removal of an organ`
    `ordinary paid work`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exploitation` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `ordinary paid work` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- trafficking in persons`

-- s 3(1): any person who "recruits, transports, transfers, harbours or receives" an individual (other than a child) by means of
-- (a) threat or use of force or other coercion; (b) abduction; (c) fraud or deception; (d) abuse of power; (e) abuse of the position
-- of vulnerability; or (f) giving or receiving money or a benefit to secure the consent of a person having control over the
-- individual, "for the purpose of the exploitation (whether in Singapore or elsewhere)" -- an offence.
-- s 3(2): for a CHILD, recruiting etc. for the purpose of exploitation is enough -- no means need be shown.
-- s 3(3): the victim's consent (or for a child, the child's or parent's or guardian's consent) "is irrelevant".
-- s 3(4): it "does not matter" that the act is done partly outside Singapore, if it would be an offence done wholly in Singapore.
DECLARE Means IS ONE OF
    `force or coercion`
    `abduction`
    `fraud or deception`
    `abuse of power`
    `abuse of the position of vulnerability`
    `paying the person in control for consent`
    `no listed means`

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `recruited, transported, transferred, harboured or received` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age of the individual` IS A NUMBER
    `means used` IS A Means
    `purpose of the conduct` IS A Purpose
    `the individual or a parent consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done partly outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the means` IS A Means
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a listed means` IF
    CONSIDER `the means`
    WHEN `no listed means` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Consent (s 3(3)) and the partly-foreign element (s 3(4)) are carried on the record but deliberately play no part.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is trafficking under s 3` IF
        `the conduct`'s `recruited, transported, transferred, harboured or received`
    AND `is exploitation` (`the conduct`'s `purpose of the conduct`)
    AND (    `is a child` (`the conduct`'s `age of the individual`)
         OR  `is a listed means` (`the conduct`'s `means used`))

§§ `4, 6, 17, 18(4), 20 -- penalties`

-- s 4(1)(a) first offence: "shall be punished with a fine not exceeding $100,000 AND with imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 10 years, and shall be liable to caning not exceeding 6 strokes"; (b) second or subsequent: $150,000, 15 years, 9 strokes.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]. s 6(2) sets the same penalties for knowingly receiving payments.
-- s 17 obstruction: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 OR to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months OR to both".
-- s 18(4) identifying a sexually-exploited victim: $5,000 or 3 years or both. s 20 false statements: $10,000 or 12 months or both.
-- INFERENCE: "second or subsequent offence" is read as an offence committed after a previous conviction for the same offence; the
-- text does not define it.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `trafficking`
    `receiving payment from exploitation`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `identifying a sexually-exploited victim`
    `a false statement`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trafficking` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 150000 ELSE 100000
    WHEN `receiving payment from exploitation` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 150000 ELSE 100000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `identifying a sexually-exploited victim` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a false statement` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trafficking` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 180 ELSE 120
    WHEN `receiving payment from exploitation` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 180 ELSE 120
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 12
    WHEN `identifying a sexually-exploited victim` THEN 36
    WHEN `a false statement` THEN 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum strokes of the cane` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trafficking` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 9 ELSE 6
    WHEN `receiving payment from exploitation` THEN IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 9 ELSE 6
    OTHERWISE 0

-- "shall be punished with a fine ... and with imprisonment": both a fine and a prison term must be imposed for ss 3 and 6.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is mandatory` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trafficking` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `receiving payment from exploitation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(2): the court "may take into account the aggravating factors ... including": (a) serious injury or death (including by suicide);
-- (b) particular vulnerability known to the offender; (c) the victim was a child; (d) exposure to a life-threatening illness;
-- (e) actual or threatened use of a weapon or drug; (f) the offender was a public servant; (g) the offender was the victim's spouse
-- or conjugal partner; (h) abuse of a position of trust or authority. The list is open ("including"); a factor off the list is not
-- excluded, only not named.
DECLARE Factor IS ONE OF
    `the victim died by suicide`
    `the victim was a child`
    `a weapon or drug was threatened`
    `the offender was a public servant`
    `the offender was the victim's conjugal partner`
    `the offender abused a position of trust`
    `the victim consented`
    `the offence lasted a long time`

GIVEN `the factor` IS A Factor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a listed aggravating factor` IF
    CONSIDER `the factor`
    WHEN `the victim consented` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the offence lasted a long time` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- abetment`

-- s 5(1): a person abets an offence under s 3 if (a) the person "instructs another person to commit the offence"; (b) "provides or
-- arranges any form of financing, transport, shelter, accommodation or any other facility WITH THE INTENTION of facilitating" it; or
-- (c) participates in the recruitment etc., employs any of the s 3(1) means, or does any act to promote the exploitation, "with the
-- intention of facilitating the commission of the offence". The intention qualifies (b) and (c), not (a).
-- s 5(2): without prejudice to "abetment" in the Penal Code generally.
GIVEN `instructed another to commit it` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided financing, transport, shelter or a facility` IS A BOOLEAN, `participated in the trafficking or exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `intended to facilitate it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `abets trafficking under s 5` IF
        `instructed another to commit it`
    OR  (    (`provided financing, transport, shelter or a facility` OR `participated in the trafficking or exploitation`)
         AND `intended to facilitate it`)

§§ `6 -- receiving payments`

-- s 6(1): "Any person who knowingly receives any payment in connection with the actual or intended exploitation IN SINGAPORE of a
-- trafficked victim" -- an offence. Contrast s 3, where the exploitation may be "in Singapore or elsewhere".
GIVEN `received a payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew of the connection` IS A BOOLEAN, `the exploitation is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 6 offence` IF
    `received a payment` AND `knew of the connection` AND `the exploitation is in Singapore`

§§ `9(3) -- detention after arrest without warrant`

-- s 9(3): a person arrested without warrant must not be detained "for longer than is reasonable in the circumstances, and such period
-- must not exceed 48 hours exclusive of the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court".
-- Only the outer limit is modelled.
GIVEN `hours held` IS A NUMBER, `hours of necessary journey` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `detention is within the 48-hour limit` IF
    `hours held` MINUS `hours of necessary journey` AT MOST 48

§§ `18 -- sexually-exploited victims`

-- s 18(1): where a person is charged with or convicted of a Part 2 offence "involving the sexual exploitation of a trafficked victim",
-- the court (a) where the victim is a child "MUST hear the matter or proceedings in private"; (b) in any other case "MAY order" a
-- private hearing. [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
-- s 18(2): no person may publish anything likely to identify the victim; (3) "regardless of whether" the hearing is in private.
DECLARE Hearing IS ONE OF
    `must be in private`
    `may be ordered in private`
    `no rule under s 18`

GIVEN `involves sexual exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `age of the victim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Hearing
`the s 18 hearing rule` MEANS
    IF NOT `involves sexual exploitation` THEN `no rule under s 18`
    ELSE IF `is a child` `age of the victim` THEN `must be in private`
         ELSE `may be ordered in private`

GIVEN `involves sexual exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `heard in private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `publishing the victim's identity is banned` IF
    `involves sexual exploitation`

§§ `21 -- informers`

-- s 21(1): no complaint as to a Part 2 offence is admitted in evidence and no witness may disclose an informer, "except as provided".
-- (3): the court may order disclosure (a) in proceedings FOR THE OFFENCE, if after full inquiry it thinks the informer "wilfully made a
-- material statement which the informer knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true"; or (b) in ANY OTHER proceedings,
-- if "justice cannot be fully done between the parties ... without the discovery of the informer".
GIVEN `proceedings for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `informer wilfully made a false material statement` IS A BOOLEAN, `justice needs the informer disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the informer disclosed` IF
    IF `proceedings for the offence`
    THEN `informer wilfully made a false material statement`
    ELSE `justice needs the informer disclosed`
